{"path":"3/library/sysconfig.html","title":"sysconfig — Provide access to Python’s configuration information","description":"Added in version 3.2.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-sysconfig"},{"type":"anchor","id":"sysconfig-provide-access-to-python-s-configuration-information"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sysconfig"},{"type":"text","value":" — Provide access to Python’s configuration information"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.2."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/sysconfig","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/sysconfig"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sysconfig"},{"type":"text","value":" module provides access to Python’s configuration information like the list of installation paths and the configuration variables relevant for the current platform."}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"configuration-variables"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Python distribution contains a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Makefile"},{"type":"text","value":" and a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"pyconfig.h"},{"type":"text","value":" header file that are necessary to build both the Python binary itself and third-party C extensions compiled using "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"setuptools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sysconfig"},{"type":"text","value":" puts all variables found in these files in a dictionary that can be accessed using "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/sysconfig.html#sysconfig.get_config_vars","title":"sysconfig.get_config_vars","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"get_config_vars()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/sysconfig.html#sysconfig.get_config_var","title":"sysconfig.get_config_var","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"get_config_var()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notice that on Windows, it’s a much smaller set."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"sysconfig.get_config_vars","term":[{"type":"text","value":"sysconfig.get_config_vars("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":"args"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With no arguments, return a dictionary of all configuration variables relevant for the current platform."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With arguments, return a list of values that result from looking up each argument in the configuration variable dictionary."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For each argument, if the value is not found, return "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"sysconfig.get_config_var","term":[{"type":"text","value":"sysconfig.get_config_var("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return the value of a single variable "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Equivalent to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"get_config_vars().get(name)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is not found, return "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example of usage:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":">>> import sysconfig\n>>> sysconfig.get_config_var('Py_ENABLE_SHARED')\n0\n>>> sysconfig.get_config_var('LIBDIR')\n'/usr/local/lib'\n>>> sysconfig.get_config_vars('AR', 'CXX')\n['ar', 'g++']"},{"type":"anchor","id":"installation-paths"},{"type":"anchor","id":"id1"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation paths"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Python uses an installation scheme that differs depending on the platform and on the installation options. These schemes are stored in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sysconfig"},{"type":"text","value":" under unique identifiers based on the value returned by "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/os.html#os.name","title":"os.name","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"os.name"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The schemes are used by package installers to determine where to copy files to."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Python currently supports nine schemes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"posix_prefix"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for POSIX platforms like Linux or macOS. This is the default scheme used when Python or a component is installed."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"posix_home"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for POSIX platforms, when the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"home"}]},{"type":"text","value":" option is used. This scheme defines paths located under a specific home prefix."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"posix_user"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for POSIX platforms, when the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"user"}]},{"type":"text","value":" option is used. This scheme defines paths located under the user’s home directory ("},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/site.html#site.USER_BASE","title":"site.USER_BASE","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"site.USER_BASE"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"posix_venv"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/venv.html#module-venv","title":"venv: Creation of virtual environments.","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Python virtual environments"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on POSIX platforms; by default it is the same as "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"posix_prefix"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nt"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for Windows. This is the default scheme used when Python or a component is installed."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nt_user"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for Windows, when the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"user"}]},{"type":"text","value":" option is used."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nt_venv"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/venv.html#module-venv","title":"venv: Creation of virtual environments.","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Python virtual environments"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on Windows; by default it is the same as "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nt"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"venv"}]},{"type":"text","value":": a scheme with values from either "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"posix_venv"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nt_venv"}]},{"type":"text","value":" depending on the platform Python runs on."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"osx_framework_user"}]},{"type":"text","value":": scheme for macOS, when the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"user"}]},{"type":"text","value":" option is used."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each scheme is itself composed of a series of paths and each path has a unique identifier. Python currently uses eight paths:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdlib"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory containing the standard Python library files that are not platform-specific."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platstdlib"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory containing the standard Python library files that are platform-specific."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platlib"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory for site-specific, platform-specific files."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"purelib"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory for site-specific, non-platform-specific files (‘pure’ Python)."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory for non-platform-specific header files for the Python C-API."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platinclude"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory for platform-specific header files for the Python C-API."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scripts"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory for script files."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"data"}]},{"type":"text","value":": directory for data files."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"user-scheme"},{"type":"anchor","id":"sysconfig-user-scheme"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"User scheme"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This scheme is designed to be the most convenient solution for users that don’t have write permission to the global site-packages directory or don’t want to install into it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files will be installed into subdirectories of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/site.html#site.USER_BASE","title":"site.USER_BASE","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"site.USER_BASE"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (written as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase"},{"type":"text","value":" hereafter). This scheme installs pure Python modules and extension modules in the same location (also known as "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/site.html#site.USER_SITE","title":"site.USER_SITE","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"site.USER_SITE"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"posix-user"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"posix_user"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation directory"}]}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/pythonX.Y"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platstdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/pythonX.Y"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/pythonX.Y/site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"purelib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/pythonX.Y/site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/include/pythonX.Y"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scripts"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/bin"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"data"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"nt-user"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"nt_user"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation directory"}]}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase\\PythonXY"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platstdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase\\PythonXY"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase\\PythonXY\\site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"purelib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase\\PythonXY\\site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase\\PythonXY\\Include"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scripts"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase\\PythonXY\\Scripts"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"data"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"osx-framework-user"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"osx_framework_user"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation directory"}]}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platstdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/python/site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"purelib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/lib/python/site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/include/pythonX.Y"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scripts"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase/bin"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"data"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"userbase"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"home-scheme"},{"type":"anchor","id":"sysconfig-home-scheme"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Home scheme"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The idea behind the “home scheme” is that you build and maintain a personal stash of Python modules. This scheme’s name is derived from the idea of a “home” directory on Unix, since it’s not unusual for a Unix user to make their home directory have a layout similar to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/local/"},{"type":"text","value":". This scheme can be used by anyone, regardless of the operating system they are installing for."}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"posix-home"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"posix_home"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation directory"}]}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home/lib/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platstdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home/lib/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home/lib/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"purelib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home/lib/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home/include/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platinclude"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home/include/python"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scripts"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home/bin"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"data"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"home"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"prefix-scheme"},{"type":"anchor","id":"sysconfig-prefix-scheme"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefix scheme"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The “prefix scheme” is useful when you wish to use one Python installation to perform the build/install (i.e., to run the setup script), but install modules into the third-party module directory of a different Python installation (or something that looks like a different Python installation). If this sounds a trifle unusual, it is—that’s why the user and home schemes come before. However, there are at least two known cases where the prefix scheme will be useful."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First, consider that many Linux distributions put Python in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr"},{"type":"text","value":", rather than the more traditional "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/local"},{"type":"text","value":". This is entirely appropriate, since in those cases Python is part of “the system” rather than a local add-on. However, if you are installing Python modules from source, you probably want them to go in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/local/lib/python2.X"},{"type":"text","value":" rather than "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/lib/python2.X"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Another possibility is a network filesystem where the name used to write to a remote directory is different from the name used to read it: for example, the Python interpreter accessed as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/local/bin/python"},{"type":"text","value":" might search for modules in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/local/lib/python2.X"},{"type":"text","value":", but those modules would have to be installed to, say, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/mnt/@server/export/lib/python2.X"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"posix-prefix"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"posix_prefix"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation directory"}]}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"prefix/lib/pythonX.Y"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platstdlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"prefix/lib/pythonX.Y"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platlib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"prefix/lib/pythonX.Y/site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"purelib"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"prefix/lib/pythonX.Y/site-packages"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"prefix/include/pythonX.Y"}]}]}]},{"cells":[{"